{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae","id":873606,"title":"Thoughts on True Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-25T01:50:40-07:00","id":873606,"title":"Thoughts on True Fae","content":"I felt that Changeling 1e had some great ideas, but never fully developed them. One idea that was mentioned in the spoiler for Changeling the Lost 1e was that the true fae love humans, are fascinated by humans, but manifests in a cruel and alien way. How-ever, I never felt that this was fully developed and could have made the True Fae into fascinating villains. For example; a true fae author lacks creativity so he puts his change-lings/ spirited away humans in circumstances and writes about how they act and react \u201cIf I turn this man\u2019s wife into a beast, will he still love her? How far is this woman willing to go to rescue her children? Will the bond of these groups of friends survive the horrors and tragedies I put in front of them?\u201d or a True Fae tries to be a prince charming that takes a plain and lonely girl and turns her into a princess. But the more beautiful and elegant she becomes, the more boring he finds her until he tosses her away to look for a new toy. Children are often stolen, because the true fae want to understand innocence or feel the joy of being a parent, but they are too selfish to really experience this.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to portray a True Fae that actually tries to help the humans it spirits, away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:11:07-07:00","id":875544,"title":"","content":"This is actually an old debate that's been thrown around a lot. Can the Gentry be benevolant? The general consensus is that while the motivations for the True Fae can be benevolant, they simply lack the empathy and understanding of the human condition to be able to pull it off in any meaningful fashion. Smothering someone with love and care ends up being overly possessive.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the True Fae are driven by selfish whims - remember that their Vritues and Vices are inverted. Their minds simply don't understand the feeling of fulfillment of helping others like humans do. To them, its a little rush, a dirty little secret, before they move on to something more fulfilling.<br /> <br /> And lets not forget that, if life really is better for a changeling in Faerie? That's a Loyalist who has no reason to leave and go home. They would never be Lost, and we wouldn't have a game set in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T14:29:01-07:00","id":879012,"title":"","content":"A True Fae who tries to help humans is totally valid. The problem is that they always misinterpret something due to being so divorced from our reality, and with so much power, the collateral damage is not limited by conventional physics. Autumn Nightmares cites Jack Skellington as an example of the chaos a True Fae can spread by trying to help.<br /> <br /> If you are very, very unlucky, you might receive an offer from a True Fae like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Manga/FrankenFran\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Franken Fran</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T15:47:26-07:00","id":879062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=879012#post879012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are very, very unlucky, you might receive an offer from a True Fae like Franken Fran .</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least Fran would be nice enough to ask first and accept a <b><i><span style=\"font-size:18px\">&quot;NO, PLEASE!&quot;</span> </i></b>(followed by the person running in abyect fear, if he/she is smart) as answer. Other Faes may take a <i>&quot;it\u00b4s for your own good&quot;</i> approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T13:14:49-07:00","id":880405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=879012#post879012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A True Fae who tries to help humans is totally valid. The problem is that they always misinterpret something due to being so divorced from our reality, and with so much power, the collateral damage is not limited by conventional physics. Autumn Nightmares cites Jack Skellington as an example of the chaos a True Fae can spread by trying to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very useful analogy, and I've extended it a bit in conversations with people. &quot;You've seen The Nightmare Before Christmas, right? Now imagine that people died and Jack never realized he did anything wrong. That's the sort of thing that happens when True Fae try to be nice.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T14:37:28-07:00","id":880483,"title":"","content":"I've always liked the idea the True Fae can love humans, but it's in the way humans love fictional characters as a result of the inherent reality divorce. So obviously they want drama to enjoy these characters they love. They may be rooting for said characters to win, but they want the narrative conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:26:31-07:00","id":880599,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hi my name is Ebony Dark\u2019ness Dementia Raven Way and I have long ebony black hair (that\u2019s how I got my name) with purple streaks and red tips that reaches my mid-back and icy blue eyes like limpid tears and I have five Titles but I wanna play changeling and be in your freehold from now on&quot;<br /> <br /> Don't offend her, preps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:39:55-07:00","id":880604,"title":"","content":"Please, even the Gentry have <i>taste</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:51:02-07:00","id":880614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=880483#post880483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always liked the idea the True Fae can love humans, but it's in the way humans love fictional characters as a result of the inherent reality divorce. So obviously they want drama to enjoy these characters they love. They may be rooting for said characters to win, but they want the narrative conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foolish Milex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=880599#post880599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Hi my name is Ebony Dark\u2019ness Dementia Raven Way and I have long ebony black hair (that\u2019s how I got my name) with purple streaks and red tips that reaches my mid-back and icy blue eyes like limpid tears and I have five Titles but I wanna play changeling and be in your freehold from now on&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Don't offend her, preps.</div> </div> </div> </div> Haruhi Suzumiya is a True Fae, confirmed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:09:27-07:00","id":880628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=880604#post880604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, even the Gentry have <i>taste</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless lack of taste is why the Fae in question is now an Exile. It would be completely a thing with them to exile someone over something like this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T20:24:17-07:00","id":880700,"title":"","content":"Maybe there's an author-kith who escaped by sabotaging their Keeper's taste. The actor now blithely intrudes upon the Freehold, protected by their degree of power and their refusal to switch to a hunting/attacking narrative, instead intruding upon every single Changeling plot they can find as &quot;the new party member&quot; and literally God-modding their way through challenges as tackily as possible, taking all the treasure and destroying all the knowledge, experience, and growth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:29:11-07:00","id":880870,"title":"","content":"Don't think about the True Fae, it only encourages them. &gt;:\\<br /> <br /> Blue / Orange morality is the default assumption most people make. In my experiences, people's durances tend towards two extremes, sometimes simultaneously. Either the Fae cares about the changeling and is just really terrifying in how that manifests or the Fae simply doesn't care about the changeling at all. In the former there is usually a narrative between the changeling and the fae. In the latter, the changeling is a human who gets caught up in a play as a prop, and it's less about the narrative and more about being a witness of the Fae and the means by which they affect their glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T16:17:37-07:00","id":885766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=879012#post879012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A True Fae who tries to help humans is totally valid. The problem is that they always misinterpret something due to being so divorced from our reality, and with so much power, the collateral damage is not limited by conventional physics. Autumn Nightmares cites Jack Skellington as an example of the chaos a True Fae can spread by trying to help.<br /> <br /> If you are very, very unlucky, you might receive an offer from a True Fae like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Manga/FrankenFran\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Franken Fran</b></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually if I recall, Fran warns people of the consequences and explains the procedure she's about to do, just like a professional doctor. She doesn't go asking people if she can perform horrendous, nightmare surgery on them. <i>They come to her and request it!</i><br /> <br /> Like this one girl who wants cosmetic surgery to look like a lolicon manga character because the boy she has a crush on is into that kind of stuff. Despite strong warnings from Fran, she insists on getting the procedure, and has to have most of her facial structure removed because manga characters have unrealistic proportions!<br /> <br /> She also has to soak herself in a medical solution every day to stop her body from dissolving.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Now if you want an example of a Fae who does horrible things while trying to help people, you may want to check out <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Manga/PetShopOfHorrors\" target=\"_blank\">Pet Shop of Horrors!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-08-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T16:53:19-07:00","id":885785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=885766#post885766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually if I recall, Fran warns people of the consequences and explains the procedure she's about to do, just like a professional doctor. She doesn't go asking people if she can perform horrendous, nightmare surgery on them. <i>They come to her and request it!</i><br /> <br /> Like this one girl who wants cosmetic surgery to look like a lolicon manga character because the boy she has a crush on is into that kind of stuff. Despite strong warnings from Fran, she insists on getting the procedure, and has to have most of her facial structure removed because manga characters have unrealistic proportions!<br /> <br /> She also has to soak herself in a medical solution every day to stop her body from dissolving.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, but she will also perform crazy procedures on people who are at risk of or already died to &quot;save&quot; them. She doesn't warn you about those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:34:38-07:00","id":885896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=885766#post885766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually if I recall, Fran warns people of the consequences and explains the procedure she's about to do, just like a professional doctor. She doesn't go asking people if she can perform horrendous, nightmare surgery on them. <i>They come to her and request it!</i><br /> <br /> Like this one girl who wants cosmetic surgery to look like a lolicon manga character because the boy she has a crush on is into that kind of stuff. Despite strong warnings from Fran, she insists on getting the procedure, and has to have most of her facial structure removed because manga characters have unrealistic proportions!<br /> <br /> She also has to soak herself in a medical solution every day to stop her body from dissolving.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------<br /> <br /> Now if you want an example of a Fae who does horrible things while trying to help people, you may want to check out <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Manga/PetShopOfHorrors\" target=\"_blank\">Pet Shop of Horrors!</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't know about that manga. It sounds like good inspirational material for a Beast who uses a similar shop as the base for a Chamber.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T21:32:51-07:00","id":885953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/873606-thoughts-on-true-fae?p=885896#post885896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn't know about that manga. It sounds like good inspirational material for a Beast who uses a similar shop as the base for a Chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually when I went back and read the TV trope thing, that's pretty much a dead on description of a True Fae! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sadly the anime only ran for four episodes, all of which can be found on Youtube if you're interested.<br /> <br /> In the anime, he sells people a Rabbit, a Mermaid, a Basilisk and a Kirin, none of which have particularly happy endings!<br /> <br /> Well, okay, the Kirin one is a matter of perspective...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-09-2016, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}